WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.840
Injuries to the head, neck, or spine are among the most serious situations you'll face because

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.240
they can affect the central nervous system.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:14.120
These injuries can be external, with obvious bleeding or swelling, but they are often internal

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:19.600
and invisible, like a concussion, which happens when the brain is rapidly shaken inside the

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.600
skull.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.799
Whether the cause is a car accident, a fall, or a sports-related collision, your assessment

00:00:25.799 --> 00:00:27.760
skills are vital here.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:33.200
If someone has a headache, feels dazed or confused, or is experiencing nausea and vomiting,

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.900
you should suspect a head injury.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:40.400
For injuries lower down, look for localized pain, bruising, or any numbness or tingling

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.919
in their arms or legs, which is a major red flag for a spine injury.

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:50.040
For severe injuries, your priorities should be to call 911 immediately and keep the person

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.880
as still as possible.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:55.320
This is the most important thing you can do to prevent further damage.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:00.919
It's also a good idea to send someone to get an AED, just in case the situation escalates.

00:01:00.919 --> 00:01:05.199
Only move them if the scene becomes unsafe or if you absolutely must perform life-saving

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:06.900
CPR.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.559
There is one other exception to the don't move them rule, and that is if the person

00:01:10.559 --> 00:01:13.400
begins to vomit and cannot clear their airway.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:18.199
In that specific case, you may need to roll them as a single unit onto their side.

00:01:18.199 --> 00:01:23.360
The goal is to keep the head, neck, and spine perfectly aligned during the roll, moving

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.199
them like a log rather than twisting any part of the body.

00:01:27.199 --> 00:01:30.000
Stay with them and keep them calm until EMS takes over.

